5595v", "ext": "mp4", "width": 720, "height": 1280, "tbr": 1427.066, "format_note": "DASH video", "container": "mp4_dash", "vcodec": "vp09.00.31.08.00.01.01.01.00", "acodec": "none", "dynamic_range": "SDR", "url": "https://instagram.fbcn12-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m367/AQPdoAzJkQvZKReMJSkANOYX17vAdi2gtRYHokRpLfsvz5YDLXqAaW7Zw6CDOZFaUrI3UKuNjKqwyXkxJ_1fnmmBpzuBUMZ3CtFE8AA.mp4?_nc_cat=111&_nc_oc=AdqrbHiRfn7NLvdW1EMazfNNTCM7sncf8631axWXzhlvS9-y-bkphLP6aWmhMGI1BXY&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fbcn12-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=xnX5hy3mr88Q7kNvwHLSNa4&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=jyPGSa9YyzBFq6gh7vHPJA&_nc_zt=28&_nc_ss=7a22e&oh=00_Af-CyRF9LD7sfqVbyuDH7iIJ9gFDzHhMMhtDJU0bUtRBwQ&oe=6A307180", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "video_ext": "mp4", "audio_ext": "none", "abr": 0, "vbr": 1427.066, "resolution": "720x1280", "aspect_ratio": 0.56, "filesize_approx": 5003293, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/144.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "format": "dash-27346951014935595v - 720x1280 (DASH video)"}], "title": "Video by kzzy47", "description": "Most people are still using AI the same way they used Google.\n\nOpen a tab. \nAsk a question. \nGet a response. \nClose it. \nLose the context. \nStart over tomorrow.\n\nThat workflow never made sense to me.\n\nThe more projects I built, the more fragmented everything became. One tool for coding. One for memory. One for research. One for workflows. One for outreach. One for organization. None of them actually understood the operation as a whole.\n\nSo I started building Pulse.\n\nAn internal operating system that connects agents, workflows, memory, content, development, research, outreach, and live business operations into one shared intelligence layer.\n\nAt the center is KRONOS.\n\nEvery workflow, conversation, system, success, failure, project, and decision feeds back into it so the operation keeps learning over time instead of resetting every session.\n\nThe craziest part is watching small teams suddenly move like companies 10x their size once repetitive operational work stops depending entirely on humans.\n\nI genuinely think most people are underestimating what happens when AI stops acting like a tool and starts acting like infrastructure.\n\nComment “PULSE” if you want to learn more about how the system works.", "duration": 28.048, "timestamp": 1779317621, "uploader_id": "1423268300", "uploader": "KZZY", "channel": "kzzy47", "like_count": 2877, "comment_count": 3081, "comments": [{"author": "matteo_060594", "author_id": "77227374621", "id": "17893653858356603", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781169261}, {"author": "sky_lo_sw", "author_id": "6659891925", "id": "18220820017320083", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781165125}, {"author": "n1ck_03", "author_id": "3205193797", "id": "17970202392064415", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781164038}, {"author": "reenasyoo", "author_id": "312782880", "id": "18008581061874282", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781163368}, {"author": "_itseliias_", "author_id": "68971286219", "id": "18445497439191822", "text": "Pulse?", "timestamp": 1781163072}, {"author": "chebanikarim", "author_id": "12668486747", "id": "18112499927478401", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781157171}, {"author": "violintotoro", "author_id": "29838356411", "id": "18010537616910009", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781151718}, {"author": "da.vid0__", "author_id": "48928794876", "id": "17885163900416451", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781135456}, {"author": "totos33", "author_id": "354175457", "id": "17915100411401973", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781125375}, {"author": "wpcplasticsk", "author_id": "66936354678", "id": "17970595104075619", "text": "Pulse", "timestamp": 1781112400}], "thumbnails": [{"ur